cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Grid Box Finder: a browser-based tool for defining and checking AutoDock Vina search boxes"
abstract: >-
  A single-file, client-side web tool that computes an AutoDock Vina / PyRx grid box
  from a co-crystallised ligand or a list of pocket residues, renders it in 3D, and runs
  automated checks for common box-definition errors - including the selection of multiple
  crystallographic copies of a ligand, which affects 9 of 25 benchmark structures, displaces the
  box centre by a median of 25 angstrom and removes the binding site from a conventionally sized
  box in 8 of 9 affected cases.
